From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 02:04:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: qrtr: Send a pending HELLO before other packets

Since 544d85de4dc2 ("net: qrtr: Send HELLO message on endpoint register"),
a packet other than HELLO fails with -EAGAIN until our HELLO has gone out,
and a work item sends that HELLO. The name server answers a remote's HELLO
by announcing the local services. If the remote's HELLO reaches it before
the work item has run, the announcement fails and is never retried:

  failed to announce new service
  failed while handling packet from 0:-2

The remote then never learns about the local services. Run the work item
before giving up on the packet.

Signed-off-by: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 net/qrtr/af_qrtr.c | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/qrtr/af_qrtr.c b/net/qrtr/af_qrtr.c
index 20460489f2..c6a965b3e6 100644
--- a/net/qrtr/af_qrtr.c
+++ b/net/qrtr/af_qrtr.c
@@ -340,6 +340,17 @@ static void qrtr_tx_flow_failed(struct qrtr_node *node, int dest_node,
 	}
 }
 
+static bool qrtr_node_hello_sent(struct qrtr_node *node)
+{
+	bool sent;
+
+	mutex_lock(&node->ep_lock);
+	sent = node->hello_sent;
+	mutex_unlock(&node->ep_lock);
+
+	return sent;
+}
+
 /* Pass an outgoing packet socket buffer to the endpoint driver. */
 static int qrtr_node_enqueue(struct qrtr_node *node, struct sk_buff *skb,
 			     int type, struct sockaddr_qrtr *from,
@@ -349,13 +360,17 @@ static int qrtr_node_enqueue(struct qrtr_node *node, struct sk_buff *skb,
 	size_t len = skb->len;
 	int rc, confirm_rx;
 
-	mutex_lock(&node->ep_lock);
-	if (!node->hello_sent && type != QRTR_TYPE_HELLO) {
-		mutex_unlock(&node->ep_lock);
-		kfree_skb(skb);
-		return -EAGAIN;
+	if (type != QRTR_TYPE_HELLO && !qrtr_node_hello_sent(node)) {
+		/*
+		 * The remote's HELLO can reach the name server before our HELLO
+		 * work has run, and the name server's reply is not retried.
+		 */
+		flush_delayed_work(&node->say_hello);
+		if (!qrtr_node_hello_sent(node)) {
+			kfree_skb(skb);
+			return -EAGAIN;
+		}
 	}
-	mutex_unlock(&node->ep_lock);
 
 	confirm_rx = qrtr_tx_wait(node, to->sq_node, to->sq_port, type);
 	if (confirm_rx < 0) {
